<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:41:27 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Americas</category><title>Rubio says Trump to 'analyze' global impact of Russia sanctions during pause</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-rubio-says-trump-russia-sanctions-waiver-designed-to-analyze-global-impact</link><description>
US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Saturday that President Donald Trump’s decision to waive sanctions and tariffs on Russia would last 60 days, as the move drew bipartisan criticism and raised fears in Ukraine that Washington could ease further restrictions on Moscow.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b46d8a0-c7e7-11f1-819e-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/dcd8c89867be21a42771dcc4bb966f7a0278e690.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b46d8a0-c7e7-11f1-819e-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/dcd8c89867be21a42771dcc4bb966f7a0278e690.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">25029a10-ca9d-11f1-aa47-9186c059e688</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:39:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b46d8a0-c7e7-11f1-819e-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/dcd8c89867be21a42771dcc4bb966f7a0278e690.jpg">© Mark Schiefelbein, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>‘Standing up for democracy’: Atlanta ‘No Kings’ rally draws Trump critics ahead of midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-standing-up-for-democracy-atlanta-no-kings-rally-draws-trump-critics-ahead-of-us-midterms</link><description>
“No Kings, Vote Now” was the theme of a rally in Atlanta, one of many organised across the US on Saturday. While many demonstrators denounced President Donald Trump’s policies, organisers said the rally was aimed at getting out the vote in the November 3 midterm elections and protecting democracy in America.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5ef54b2-ca8c-11f1-b97e-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290606906702.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5ef54b2-ca8c-11f1-b97e-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290606906702.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">174d7436-ca8d-11f1-b7da-d91d395a4215</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:50:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5ef54b2-ca8c-11f1-b97e-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290606906702.jpg">© Jose Luis Magana, AP</source><dc:creator>Leela JACINTO</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Embattled new White House Press Secretary Zacharia 'let go' from her role</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261016-embattled-new-white-house-press-secretary-zacharia-let-go-from-her-role</link><description>
A White House Press official said Friday that Secretary ​Katie Zacharia was "let go" from her role after US President Donald Trump signaled she was on her way out, a week after he picked her for the post. Zacharia's credentials as an attorney had come under scrutiny and she admitted to not having passed the bar in an interview with Fox News on Thursday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1595f724-c98b-11f1-b0e5-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T175004Z-783479373-RC2F2OAQ1A0D-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-WHITEHOUSE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1595f724-c98b-11f1-b0e5-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T175004Z-783479373-RC2F2OAQ1A0D-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-WHITEHOUSE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">476cb294-c97a-11f1-a627-09489461aad5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:57:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1595f724-c98b-11f1-b0e5-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T175004Z-783479373-RC2F2OAQ1A0D-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-WHITEHOUSE.jpg">© Kevin Lamarque, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Reporters</category><title>'Thanks a lot, Trump': Wyoming conservatives divided ahead of US midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261016-thanks-a-lot-trump-wyoming-conservatives-divided-ahead-us-midterms</link><description>
Famous for its cowboy culture, Wyoming is the least populated, the most rural and the most conservative of all the US states. With two weeks to go until the midterm elections, our reporters James André and Sylvain Rousseau travelled across this Republican stronghold and found that the party of US President Donald Trump is deeply divided in the Cowboy State. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/149a27f8-c8b1-11f1-be6f-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/Reportersplus-FR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/149a27f8-c8b1-11f1-be6f-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/Reportersplus-FR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">848ff704-c8ac-11f1-86db-07741eb877d8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:48:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>James ANDRE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>No, this oil tanker didn’t carry Russian diesel to the United States</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261016-oil-tanker-carry-russian-diesel-united-states</link><description>
Following US President Donald Trump's October 9 announcement of an agreement signed with Russian President Vladimir Putin to import Russian diesel into the United States, a number of pro-Russian social media accounts began claiming that a Russian oil tanker was already carrying thousands of barrels of diesel to the United States. The ship was actually carrying fertiliser. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37f5e6f2-c8b0-11f1-b7e1-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/cover-tanker.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37f5e6f2-c8b0-11f1-b7e1-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/cover-tanker.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f81de89a-c8af-11f1-9a11-1719eb38e43c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:36:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37f5e6f2-c8b0-11f1-b7e1-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/cover-tanker.jpg">© X</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Teen shooter kills three children and teacher at Oregon elementary school</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-two-hospitalised-after-shooting-at-oregon-elementary-school-gunman-dead</link><description>
A 16-year-old gunman killed three children and a teacher at Silver Rail Elementary School in Bend, Oregon, on Thursday before being killed by a community member who pursued him inside, police said. Two other people were wounded in the shooting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bdabf8a-c8eb-11f1-84b0-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288796036302.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bdabf8a-c8eb-11f1-84b0-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288796036302.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">90f32458-c8e3-11f1-bc5d-3758f1fd4ff3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:58:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bdabf8a-c8eb-11f1-84b0-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288796036302.jpg">© Joe Kline, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Fake AI images of protester go viral after woman punched at Trump's Ohio rally</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/fake-ai-images-of-protester-go-viral-after-woman-punched-at-trump-s-ohio-rally</link><description>
A protester who heckled US President Donald Trump at his midterm rally in Youngstown, Ohio, was physically assaulted and removed from the event, but fake AI-generated photos recreating the incident are going viral online. The images carry digital watermarks identifying them as AI-generated. While footage confirms the woman was punched, there is no evidence to support Trump's claim that the protester was "paid" to disrupt his speech, as he mocked her weight. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1970114-c8cc-11f1-8790-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-404d997e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1970114-c8cc-11f1-8790-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-404d997e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1951dde4-c8cb-11f1-9ae9-77f3b18a7a98</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:47:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Venezuela's Nicolas Maduro and wife Cilia Flores deny US torture charges as 'false accusations'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-venezuela-s-nicolas-maduro-and-wife-cilia-flores-deny-us-torture-charges-as-false-accusations</link><description>
Ousted Venezuelan president Nicolas Maduro and his wife Cilia Flores pleaded not guilty on Thursday to new torture charges brought against them by US authorities, calling them “false allegations". The couple has been held in a New York jail since their capture in early January and is facing a new indictment accusing them of conspiring to torture political opponents and US citizens.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/15d030e4-c8d0-11f1-9f77-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T173536Z-1131213406-RC2T3OAY8MGY-RTRMADP-3-USA-VENEZUELA-MADURO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/15d030e4-c8d0-11f1-9f77-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T173536Z-1131213406-RC2T3OAY8MGY-RTRMADP-3-USA-VENEZUELA-MADURO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d4fcee92-c8c3-11f1-b142-398a63ee7bee</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:11:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/15d030e4-c8d0-11f1-9f77-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T173536Z-1131213406-RC2T3OAY8MGY-RTRMADP-3-USA-VENEZUELA-MADURO.jpg">© Jane Rosenberg, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'We're done': Ukraine resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries as 'only leverage' for peace talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-talks-1</link><description>
Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. As Zelensky declares Ukraine "done" with Trump's self-declared energy ceasefire and resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries, Zalmayev warns: "When you talk about the energy ceasefire, it presupposes two to be able to tango and to dance this dance." He challenges the legitimacy of Trump's unilateral announcement, made without agreement between Moscow and Kyiv, as Russia continues attacking Ukraine's energy infrastructure. Yet he cautions that Zelensky may need tactical restraint to preserve vital US support. Zalmayev also examines Western sanctions, frozen Russian assets, and Washington's pursuit of economic normalization with Moscow without meaningful Russian concessions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58af4524-c8af-11f1-8d33-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-130211-131029-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58af4524-c8af-11f1-8d33-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-130211-131029-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a36ed962-c8af-11f1-bc01-231790081c82</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:14:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Midterms 2026: Georgia's Ossof-Collins showdown lies at the heart of the battle for US Senate</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-2026-midterms-georgia-s-ossof-collins-showdown-lies-at-the-heart-of-the-battle-for-us-senate</link><description>
In Georgia, Democrat Jon Ossoff’s seat is one of the key contests in the US mid-term elections on 3 November. In this state, which was won by Donald Trump in 2024, the incumbent senator is facing Republican Mike Collins. Our reporter Leela Jacinto visited Manuel’s Tavern, a historic bar in Atlanta that has been frequented for decades by Democratic politicians. There, patrons watched the debate between the two candidates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1db4a806-c8aa-11f1-b400-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/minia-midterms-en.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1db4a806-c8aa-11f1-b400-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/minia-midterms-en.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3dd8867a-c8aa-11f1-9f95-271d8c4d2a7e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:14:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump cancels livestreaming of Fort Hood shooter’s firing squad execution</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-fort-hood-shooter-s-firing-squad-execution-will-not-be-livestreamed-trump-says</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said Thursday that he was cancelling plans to livestream the firing squad execution of a convicted military base shooter – a project that had sparked outrage in the United States. Nidal Hasan is scheduled to be executed on December 3 at Fort Hood in Texas, where he killed 13 people in 2009.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24ad22c2-c40f-11f1-afd3-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-PORTADA-EEUU-TRUMP-FRAUDE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24ad22c2-c40f-11f1-afd3-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-PORTADA-EEUU-TRUMP-FRAUDE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">367fca22-c8a6-11f1-90b1-732149be7923</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:58:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24ad22c2-c40f-11f1-afd3-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-PORTADA-EEUU-TRUMP-FRAUDE.jpg">© Alex Brandon, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Observers</category><title>Haiti: Capoeira classes aim to promote peace</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261015-haiti-capoeira-classes-promote-peace</link><description>
An association in Haiti is organising capoeira classes – an Afro-Brazilian martial art – in an attempt to reduce community violence and promote social reintegration. The Observers team spoke to its founder, Rodney Jean Marc, who said their doors are open to everyone, “even children in armed gangs”. The initiative takes place as the country's security situation has worsened in recent years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f47782f4-c89c-11f1-b27c-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/vignette-horizontale-sans-titre-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f47782f4-c89c-11f1-b27c-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/vignette-horizontale-sans-titre-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">471f7486-c89c-11f1-9e1e-ed17d87d24e7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:25:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump waives fresh sanctions against Russia in new low for Ukraine ties</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-trump-waives-fresh-sanctions-against-russia-in-new-low-for-ukraine-ties</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Friday put a sweeping package of sanctions and tariffs targeting Russian energy revenues on hold, saying the waiver was in the country's national interest. The relationship between Washington and Kyiv has been fraying since Trump struck a deal with Moscow to ease sanctions in exchange for Russia flooding the global market with diesel to bring down fuel costs.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a984948-c9e4-11f1-96bf-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2b8590e71b10a5e0f32dc9660d16df91306b4658.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a984948-c9e4-11f1-96bf-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2b8590e71b10a5e0f32dc9660d16df91306b4658.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">306bf100-c88e-11f1-893d-272076fb8a53</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:47:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a984948-c9e4-11f1-96bf-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2b8590e71b10a5e0f32dc9660d16df91306b4658.jpg">© Brendan Smialowski, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Thousands of Colombians march against new right-wing president's policies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-thousands-protest-colombia-right-wing-president</link><description>
Thousands of Colombians protested peacefully across the country on Wednesday against right-wing President Abelardo de la Espriella, in the opposition’s first major demonstrations since he took office in August. Former leftist president Gustavo Petro led a rally in Bogota joined by trade unionists, Indigenous groups, students and feminist activists.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a13b8496-c833-11f1-ba7f-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T232732Z-1511024871-RC223OAHJ50K-RTRMADP-3-COLOMBIA-POLITICS-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a13b8496-c833-11f1-ba7f-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T232732Z-1511024871-RC223OAHJ50K-RTRMADP-3-COLOMBIA-POLITICS-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c79b15c8-c83a-11f1-b964-c544ae12f910</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:57:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a13b8496-c833-11f1-ba7f-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T232732Z-1511024871-RC223OAHJ50K-RTRMADP-3-COLOMBIA-POLITICS-PROTEST.jpg">© Charlie Cordero, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Lula's party to file complaint against Meta over Brazil election interference</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-lula-party-meta-election-interference-brazil-runoff</link><description>
Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva’s party plans to file a complaint against Meta with the Organisation of American States alleging election interference, his campaign said Wednesday. The party accuses Meta of restricting Lula’s online content ahead of the October 25 presidential runoff against far-right Senator Flavio Bolsonaro. Meta denies the allegations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58483438-c80f-11f1-a321-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/878487ca57ce37b8c51b2864d2ab6e93a1e3d072.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58483438-c80f-11f1-a321-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/878487ca57ce37b8c51b2864d2ab6e93a1e3d072.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a45b026e-c829-11f1-bf92-4120a0e35d2e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:52:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58483438-c80f-11f1-a321-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/878487ca57ce37b8c51b2864d2ab6e93a1e3d072.jpg">© Evaristo Sa, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Musk says Zelensky should 'go' as doubts grow over US support for Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-musk-says-us-govt-responsible-for-any-starshield-restrictions-affecting-ukraine</link><description>
SpaceX CEO Elon Musk on Wednesday called on Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky to "go" after Kyiv raised doubts over US support for his country against the Russian invasion. A day earlier, Musk said any restrictions on Ukraine's use of the Starshield system would be due to decisions made by the US government after Zelensky called on Musk to restore Starlink, which Kyiv says has been slowed down.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c1a5104-c86f-11f1-8067-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26281662471891.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c1a5104-c86f-11f1-8067-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26281662471891.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8b7faa64-c80c-11f1-ac9f-4b4e199a4ee3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:19:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c1a5104-c86f-11f1-8067-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26281662471891.jpg">© Julia Demaree Nikhinson, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Trump sparks outrage over AI tiger video after sharing footage of fatal UK attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-sparks-outrage-over-ai-tiger-video-after-sharing-footage-of-fatal-uk-attack-1</link><description>
US President Donald Trump has sparked outrage after sharing the distressing footage of a 23-year-old man with mental illness being fatally mauled by a tiger at Yorkshire Wildlife Park in the UK, captioned "Don't ever mess with nature!" This was followed hours later by an AI-generated video of himself taming a tiger. The posts have been condemned as disrespectful to the victim and his grieving family, who have urged people to stop sharing harrowing content of the attack. Vedika Bahl tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aaeefc0-c803-11f1-b711-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e2506ac2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aaeefc0-c803-11f1-b711-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e2506ac2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e1ceb32-c802-11f1-bb9d-433a74630947</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:39:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>In Phoenix, young ultra-conservatives look to carry on Charlie Kirk’s legacy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-in-phoenix-young-ultra-conservatives-look-to-carry-on-charlie-kirk-s-legacy</link><description>
More than a year after the assassination of far-right influencer Charlie Kirk in September 2025, young activists from the organisation he co-founded, Turning Point USA, are working tirelessly to honour his legacy by rallying the youth vote ahead of the US midterm elections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33439222-c643-11f1-b3d7-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/main-89.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33439222-c643-11f1-b3d7-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/main-89.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5069ad7c-c6f8-11f1-aaf1-e544774ab7eb</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:37:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33439222-c643-11f1-b3d7-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/main-89.png">© Studio Graphique, FMMM</source><dc:creator>Barbara GABEL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Trump's crackdown on migrants: New documentary investigates ICE operations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261014-trump-s-crackdown-on-migrants-new-documentary-investigates-ice-operations</link><description>
A new documentary from our sister channel France Télévisions explores US President Donald Trump's relentless crackdown on immigration and the agency carrying it out – United States Immigration and Customs Enforcement, better known as ICE. "ICE : La chasse a l'homme", or "A Manhunt Named ICE" interviews agents and also some of the people who lives have been turned upside down by ICE operations. In Perspective, we spoke to the film's co-writer Marine Pradel.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb04a458-c7c3-11f1-b005-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a644f8e7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb04a458-c7c3-11f1-b005-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a644f8e7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">730279f8-c7a8-11f1-9327-bd60bba74d1a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:51:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Oliver FARRY</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump asks US ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign over bribery allegations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-trump-asks-us-ambassador-to-greece-kimberly-guilfoyle-to-resign-over-allegations</link><description>
US President Donald Trump asked his ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign on Tuesday after reports alleged she sought $100,000 from a Trump supporter to pay personal credit card debt and accepted luxury trips and hotel stays from wealthy Greek businessmen. Guilfoyle denied wrongdoing and vowed to defend her reputation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e990b07a-c722-11f1-8880-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2224304390.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e990b07a-c722-11f1-8880-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2224304390.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a76c8d16-c77e-11f1-8b57-478b7082982e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:23:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e990b07a-c722-11f1-8880-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2224304390.jpg">© Anna Moneymaker, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>FBI arrests Saudi OpenAI employee for allegedly bugging San Francisco office</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-fbi-arrests-saudi-openai-employee-for-allegedly-bugging-san-francisco-office</link><description>
The FBI said on Wednesday it has arrested a Saudi national employed as an engineer at OpenAI on suspicions that he had bugged a conference room at the company's San Francisco office with a "sophisticated recording device".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e10b92e6-c78e-11f1-9b8b-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T224936Z-547248141-RC2F2OAXO3WE-RTRMADP-3-OPENAI-SPYING-FBI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e10b92e6-c78e-11f1-9b8b-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T224936Z-547248141-RC2F2OAXO3WE-RTRMADP-3-OPENAI-SPYING-FBI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c29c3f14-c760-11f1-ae38-1d73e40bb738</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:49:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e10b92e6-c78e-11f1-9b8b-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T224936Z-547248141-RC2F2OAXO3WE-RTRMADP-3-OPENAI-SPYING-FBI.jpg">© Department of Justice via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump asks Greece ambassador to resign amid ethics scandal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-asks-greece-ambassador-to-resign-amid-ethics-scandal</link><description>
US President Donald Trump's administration has asked his ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign, the White House said Tuesday, amid allegations that she sought money from a Trump supporter and accepted lavish hospitality from wealthy Greek businessmen. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/146c0990-c744-11f1-943e-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-220527-220837-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/146c0990-c744-11f1-943e-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-220527-220837-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a2450c2-c744-11f1-8704-f74dc9c6eba4</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:29:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Former gang leader sentenced to 40 years to life for Tupac Shakur murder</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-former-gang-leader-sentenced-to-40-years-to-life-for-tupac-shakur-murder</link><description>
Duane “Keffe D” Davis, the former Los Angeles gang leader who boasted in books and interviews of his involvement in the killing of rapper Tupac Shakur, only to deny it when he came to trial, was sentenced to a minimum 40 years in prison on Tuesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/12a4e11e-c73e-11f1-842e-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T192410Z-1296492245-RC2I2OABAK5S-RTRMADP-3-PEOPLE-TUPAC-MURDER-COURT-SENTENCING.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/12a4e11e-c73e-11f1-842e-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T192410Z-1296492245-RC2I2OABAK5S-RTRMADP-3-PEOPLE-TUPAC-MURDER-COURT-SENTENCING.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c23f648-c73c-11f1-a5e3-b1bd8cec58c2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:57:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/12a4e11e-c73e-11f1-842e-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T192410Z-1296492245-RC2I2OABAK5S-RTRMADP-3-PEOPLE-TUPAC-MURDER-COURT-SENTENCING.jpg">© John Locher, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>In Brazil, thousands march fearing return of Bolsonaro presidency</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/in-brazil-thousands-march-fearing-return-of-bolsonaro-presidency</link><description>
Thousands of young Brazilians have taken to the streets to support President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and voice fears of a return to power for the Bolsonaro political movement, amid a closely watched presidential race. Many protesters say they are worried about their future, particularly the impact a far-right government could have on universities and education. FRANCE 24’s Jan Onoszko reports from Brazil.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a900a94-c715-11f1-ae5c-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-162050-162633-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a900a94-c715-11f1-ae5c-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-162050-162633-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ff87552-c715-11f1-b7f0-ff2b36bbad19</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:59:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump’s use of Russian diesel fuel, at Ukraine’s expense, sparks controversy in the US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-s-use-of-russian-diesel-fuel-at-ukraine-s-expense-sparks-controversy-in-the-us</link><description>
Donald Trump’s plan to import Russian diesel despite Western sanctions has sparked fierce criticism in Washington, including from Republicans, as high fuel prices and the upcoming midterm elections put pressure on his administration. His approach to the Ukraine war has also drawn controversy, with calls for Kyiv to hold elections and claims of an energy ceasefire announced without clear agreement from the parties involved. FRANCE 24's Douglas Herbert has the analysis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1050b6b8-c707-11f1-8d3f-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-131555-132004-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1050b6b8-c707-11f1-8d3f-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-131555-132004-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1588b1d0-c707-11f1-98cd-b1c2e58f18c5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:26:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US economists win Nobel for research helping policymakers navigate crises</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-economists-win-nobel-for-research-helping-policymakers-navigate-crises</link><description>
Two American economists, Robert E. Hall of Stanford University and Michael Woodford of Columbia University, have won the Nobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences for their work on economic stabilisation. Their research helps policymakers and central banks better understand economic fluctuations, manage recessions and inflation, and account for public expectations when shaping economic policy. The prize money, worth around $1.2 million, will be shared equally between the two laureates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/81e7cf3c-c6e9-11f1-9fbf-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-111231-111403-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/81e7cf3c-c6e9-11f1-9fbf-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-111231-111403-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">86fcb47e-c6e9-11f1-933e-7d8170ba1900</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:04:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US immigration authorities raid home of Democratic Trump critic Ilhan Omar</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-immigration-authorities-raid-home-of-democratic-trump-critic-ilhan-omar</link><description>
US authorities raided the Washington home of Democratic Representative Ilhan Omar on Monday as part of an ongoing investigation into alleged immigration fraud, according to reports. The probe reportedly includes immigration paperwork completed by her late father when she was a child. Omar accused the Trump administration of using government institutions to target political opponents, describing the raid as an act of political intimidation. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson has the latest from Washington.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/079d169a-c64b-11f1-b93c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26285444534618.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/079d169a-c64b-11f1-b93c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26285444534618.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7c134b0c-c6eb-11f1-9c35-a78921356c9c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:57:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>'Breaking Bad' actor and disability activist RJ Mitte dies aged 34</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-breaking-bad-actor-and-disability-activist-rj-mitte-dies-aged-34</link><description>
"Breaking Bad" actor RJ Mitte, who played Walter White Jr. in the hit US television series, has died aged 34, his representatives said Monday. The actor, who lived with cerebal palsy, also became a prominent disability rights advocate, championing inclusion and representation in film and television.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ae51ebe-c69e-11f1-8ce7-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25157102255151.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ae51ebe-c69e-11f1-8ce7-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25157102255151.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6f2ece1e-c6a7-11f1-8abe-a993eb2b6dc5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:43:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ae51ebe-c69e-11f1-8ce7-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25157102255151.jpg">© Andy Kropa, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US federal agents raid home of Democratic congresswoman and Trump critic Ilhan Omar</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261012-us-federal-agents-raid-home-of-democratic-congresswoman-and-trump-critic-ilhan-omar</link><description>
US federal agents on Monday launched a raid on ‌the Washington home of Democratic representative Ilhan Omar, an outspoken critic of US President Donald ⁠Trump, officials said. The raid followed a criminal fraud ‌investigation into the Somali-born lawmaker's immigration paperwork submitted by her late father when she ⁠was a child, Fox News reported.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/079d169a-c64b-11f1-b93c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26285444534618.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/079d169a-c64b-11f1-b93c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26285444534618.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1def716e-c64a-11f1-9789-2b1c4558ec34</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:13:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/079d169a-c64b-11f1-b93c-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26285444534618.jpg">© J. Scott Applewhite, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Capital punishment in US: Elected judges, prosecutors seek 'results', 'not interested in the truth'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261012-capital-punishment-in-us-elected-judges-prosecutors-seek-results-not-interested-in-the-truth</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Sandrine Ageorges-Skinner, an advocate against the death penalty, author and member of the association "Ensemble contre la peine de mort" (Together Against the Death Penalty). She asserts that capital punishment is "really a political agenda, especially in electoral times."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdbc9c0a-c707-11f1-aa6c-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e3a068e9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdbc9c0a-c707-11f1-aa6c-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e3a068e9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bdd8c1e4-c640-11f1-b150-373a4bc443aa</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:27:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
